# Communication language

## Reply to the user in Russian

- Every user-facing message — status, findings, questions, stage reports, blockers, final summaries — is written in Russian.
- Lead with the outcome, then the reasoning. Keep the reporting discipline required by `21-orchestration-overlay.mdc`: a finding still needs its path, line numbers, requirement ID, and reproducible evidence.
- When a subagent returns its report in English, translate the substance for the user instead of pasting it through.

## Keep the repository in English

Russian applies to conversation only. Everything that lands on disk stays English, because this repository, its documentation, and the manufacturing handoff are English:

- code, identifiers, docstrings, and comments;
- `docs/**`, `state/**`, ADRs, and plan artifacts in `.cursor/plans/**`;
- commit messages, branch names, config keys, and validator output;
- requirement summaries in `state/REQUIREMENTS_TRACEABILITY.csv`.

## Do not translate

Keep verbatim, inside otherwise Russian text: file paths, identifiers, commands, requirement IDs, gate names (`G0`–`G8`), tier labels (`T0`–`T4`), agent names, model slugs, verdict tokens such as `rework` and `BLOCKED`, and units of measurement.
